// stdlib_array_arg — array-typed arguments must not pass the stdlib call
// type check. EvalDataType of an array expression returns the ELEMENT
// kind, so without the IsArrayTypedBase guard `int[]` masqueraded as int
// and math.sqrt reinterpreted the array handle as a float (Step 0 review
// MAJOR regression guard).
int main() {
    int[] arr = new int[3];
    float f = math.sqrt(arr);
    return 0;
}
